<header><h1>Victory Points: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_victory_points">Victory Points</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>During the action phase, if multiple players gain victory points at the same time, they gain them in <a href="/R_initiative_order">initiative order</a>, starting with the player who has the lowest initiative number, regardless of who the active player is.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the Xxcha hero gives two players in the lead a Victory Point, and both players now have enough points to win the game, is the order for winning determined from Xxcha player (active player) onwards in initiative, or starting with the lowest initiatve? A: Initiative order determines the winner. Initiative order is always the lowest initiative player onwards, regardless of who the active player is.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During the agenda phase, if multiple players gain victory points at the same time, they gain them in speaker order, starting with the <a href="/R_speaker">speaker</a> and proceeding clockwise.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;In what order are agenda-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;In speaker order, clockwise; it only matters if several players would win from the points, a tie that also goes clockwise from the speaker.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player can lose victory points. For example, a player who has another player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Support_for_the_Throne"><i>Support for the Throne</i></a> promissory note in their play area loses one victory point when it is returned.<sup>3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Support for the Throne: &ldquo;If you activate a system that contains 1 or more of the blue player&rsquo;s units, or if the blue player is eliminated, lose 1 victory point and return this card to the blue player.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
